generated C sources have drifted from their generators — `make regenerate` is
DESTRUCTIVE.

SYMPTOM
Running `make -C sources regenerate` (host CL) produces files that DELETE
hand-applied fixes present in the committed generated sources:
- built_in_functions.c: kernel_TYPEP's symbol-type-specifier resolution;
  kernel_SET_SYMBOL_{VALUE,FUNCTION,PLIST} argument order (the generated code
  passes (symbol, value) to C functions taking (value, symbol)); the
  bytecode.h/packages.h includes.
- kernel_structure_functions.{c,h}: the v1.7.2 hot-3 CONS representation of
  LEXICAL-VARIABLE (regenerates as a structure instance — a performance
  regression AND an ABI change vs env_lexical_variable_p==consp callers);
  the v1.7.1 _fast accessors.
- structure_functions.c: the GC-rootset push of the structure classes in
  kernel_initialize_structure_functions (regenerating removes kernel_classes
  pinning — a GC hazard).
Also environmental: the generators need com.informatimago.common-lisp.cesarum
via quicklisp + a hard-coded ~/src/public/com-informatimago/ registry path.

HOW FOUND (v1.8.36): adding the ENV slot to LOCAL-FUNCTION for the FLET
conformance fix; regeneration had to be reverted and the slot applied by hand
to the four generated files (generate-structures.lisp WAS updated, so the
spec is current for that structure).

FIX OPTIONS
a) Teach the generators the hand fixes (TYPEP resolution, setter argument
   order, cons-represented lexical variables, _fast accessors, rootset
   pushes) so regeneration is faithful; or
b) stop committing generator output for the drifted files and treat the C as
   the source of truth (retire the generators); or
c) split: keep generators for the mechanical parts, move the hand-fixed
   functions out of the generated files.
Until then: NEVER run `make regenerate` and commit blindly — diff against the
committed files and keep every hand fix.
